.TH TT 6.SH NAMEtt \- Tetris for terminals.SH SYNOPSIS\fBtt\fR[\-s] [\-b] [\-l\fIn\fR].SH DESCRIPTIONTetris in a character well, by Mike Taylor.  Pieces fall and you steerthem to fill whole rows, which vanish.  The keys:.TP 12\fB,\fRmove left..TP 12\fB/\fRmove right..TP 12\fB.\fRrotate..TP 12\fIspace\fRdrop..TP 12\fBs\fRpause..TP 12\fBq\fRquit..TP 12\fB^L\fRredraw the screen..PPThe score, the pieces and the levels so far are shown beside the well..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-s\fRprint the high-score table and leave..TP 12\fB\-l\fIn\fRstart at level\fIn\fR,\fRfrom \-10 to 20..PPThe usage line also lists\fB\-b\fR.\fR.SH ENVIRONMENT.TP 12\fBTTNAME\fRthe name the score table records..TP 12\fBTTKEYS\fRother keys in place of the ones above..SH FILES.TP 12\fB/h0/games/lib/ttscores\fRthe high scores..SH SEE ALSOtypefast